WEBVTT

00:15.750 --> 00:17.350
How did you get hurt so badly?

00:18.210 --> 00:19.470
What is the situation?

00:20.330 --> 00:21.550
Met someone useless.

00:22.270 --> 00:24.180
Mo Yungao didn't show up at all.

00:24.330 --> 00:25.640
But just as I guessed,

00:25.830 --> 00:27.760
they have already made their move.

00:28.910 --> 00:31.040
That group is trickier than I thought.

00:54.750 --> 00:56.600
They already know I am Miss Dong.

00:56.600 --> 00:59.330
They might attack
the Dong Residence right away.

01:06.140 --> 01:08.840
I missed you so much,

01:09.180 --> 01:11.050
Miss Dong.

01:11.080 --> 01:12.410
You are not Mo Yungao.

01:15.760 --> 01:17.560
Take everyone in the Dong family

01:17.880 --> 01:19.150
and leave Xiacheng now.

01:19.150 --> 01:20.880
It's best to leave the country.

01:21.390 --> 01:22.720
This is the concession.

01:23.010 --> 01:24.740
No one dares to make a move here.

01:24.940 --> 01:25.940
Besides,

01:25.970 --> 01:28.000
you are the daughter
of the Ship King.

01:28.000 --> 01:28.930
In Xiacheng,

01:29.730 --> 01:31.850
no one can touch you.

01:33.720 --> 01:34.920
If a gun is fired here,

01:35.220 --> 01:38.160
friends from other consulates
will send troops.

01:38.789 --> 01:40.789
Rest and recover with peace of mind.

01:41.430 --> 01:42.890
It's different this time.

01:43.229 --> 01:45.090
This time we are facing a warlord.

01:45.840 --> 01:47.259
That Lu Junxiang, too—

01:48.520 --> 01:50.660
he will definitely try
every possible means to kill me.

01:50.660 --> 01:51.740
Lu Junxiang?

01:52.450 --> 01:54.910
A prisoner captured
at the Archives before.

01:58.720 --> 01:59.380
No.

02:01.310 --> 02:02.910
You must leave immediately.

02:07.930 --> 02:10.000
I won't leave you behind.

02:14.450 --> 02:15.330
Mr. Dong.

02:16.050 --> 02:17.360
I was just using you.

02:18.160 --> 02:20.800
Back then,
I needed this identity to protect myself.

02:20.800 --> 02:23.060
There's not much time left
for you to run.

02:31.220 --> 02:33.350
I didn't expect him to come so quickly.

02:33.970 --> 02:35.630
I really underestimated him.

04:09.240 --> 04:15.340
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

04:15.700 --> 04:18.339
[Episode 13]

04:26.270 --> 04:27.810
Why is there nothing?

04:30.890 --> 04:34.530
[Six hours left]

04:36.750 --> 04:37.480
Plague.

04:38.070 --> 04:38.810
Plague?

04:40.250 --> 04:40.990
Plague!

04:41.409 --> 04:42.560
I finally found you.

04:42.560 --> 04:43.120
Why are you here?

04:43.120 --> 04:44.510
Do you know how hard I looked for you?

04:44.510 --> 04:45.920
I have something important to tell you.

04:45.920 --> 04:46.800
Whatever you're saying right now,

04:46.800 --> 04:47.600
I can't hear it.

04:47.600 --> 04:49.430
I have something very important
to do right now.

04:49.430 --> 04:51.010
-Hey.
-Time is running out.

04:51.010 --> 04:52.159
I-I know.

04:52.159 --> 04:53.760
I have something to give you.

04:54.120 --> 04:54.860
Money!

04:55.430 --> 04:56.250
Listen to me!

04:56.480 --> 04:57.430
It's money!

04:58.240 --> 04:58.659
Your friend—

04:58.659 --> 04:59.430
Get lost.

05:02.540 --> 05:03.420
Zhang Hailou!

05:04.240 --> 05:05.930
I don't care what you're doing.

05:05.930 --> 05:07.290
What could be so important

05:07.290 --> 05:10.890
that it's more important
than what your dead friend left behind?

05:12.540 --> 05:13.750
These are the things your friend

05:13.750 --> 05:15.780
asked me to give you before he died.

05:16.480 --> 05:18.190
I guess there's very important information
on this,

05:18.190 --> 05:20.250
which is why I turned back to find you.

05:21.360 --> 05:22.100
You keep it.

05:24.090 --> 05:25.550
This is Shrimpie's money.

05:27.050 --> 05:28.340
I don't know who he is.

05:29.030 --> 05:31.560
Anyway, your friend asked me
to give it to you.

05:31.750 --> 05:32.750
Why do you have it?

05:32.970 --> 05:34.290
It was on the ship.

05:34.659 --> 05:36.600
Your friend slipped it to me

05:36.600 --> 05:37.830
in a very chaotic situation.

05:37.830 --> 05:39.240
He told me to give it to his partner.

05:39.240 --> 05:41.370
How was I supposed to know that was you?

05:41.480 --> 05:42.810
But whatever happened in between,

05:42.810 --> 05:43.570
I have no idea.

05:43.570 --> 05:44.770
Anyway, by coincidence,

05:44.770 --> 05:46.210
things have come to this.

05:46.540 --> 05:47.920
There must be some

05:47.920 --> 05:49.420
important hidden information on it.

05:49.420 --> 05:50.620
That's why I came back

05:50.620 --> 05:52.080
to find you in such a hurry.

05:56.370 --> 05:56.909
You...

05:57.380 --> 05:59.640
Why didn't I keep an eye on him
on the ship?

06:00.800 --> 06:01.420
All right.

06:02.070 --> 06:02.890
Hurry up and see

06:02.890 --> 06:05.420
if there's anything important
on this money.

06:11.600 --> 06:13.020
Two-square cipher.

06:15.010 --> 06:17.780
Is this a military decryption method?

06:18.120 --> 06:19.690
As long as you have
the key and the ciphertext,

06:19.690 --> 06:21.490
you can decipher the words on it.

06:24.740 --> 06:25.870
You know about this?

06:26.540 --> 06:27.560
I don't.

06:28.040 --> 06:29.930
It's you—you're a lucky guy.

06:31.320 --> 06:32.880
God is watching over you.

06:33.450 --> 06:34.670
When I was looking for you,

06:34.670 --> 06:36.060
I ran into a bunch of robbers.

06:36.060 --> 06:37.620
I almost died there.

06:40.360 --> 06:41.020
Patrolman!

06:41.070 --> 06:42.000
Right here!

06:42.060 --> 06:43.070
Someone is committing robbery here!

06:43.070 --> 06:44.040
Take it, take it.

06:44.630 --> 06:46.430
Luckily, I met a kind-hearted person.

06:46.430 --> 06:47.250
She saved me.

06:53.970 --> 06:56.970
[Wesley, Haili Bank Manager]

06:54.100 --> 06:55.810
She is the manager of Haili Bank.

06:55.810 --> 06:57.480
Her father was a foreign soldier.

06:57.480 --> 06:58.980
That's how I know all this.

06:59.360 --> 07:00.250
The code on this money

07:00.250 --> 07:02.000
should be a two-square cipher.

07:02.000 --> 07:04.980
Generally, only people
in special military and political work

07:04.980 --> 07:05.680
would use it.

07:05.680 --> 07:07.560
It's mainly used
to transmit important intelligence.

07:07.450 --> 07:10.280
[Haili Bank]

07:08.130 --> 07:10.230
It was also her
who mobilized everyone in Haili Bank

07:10.230 --> 07:11.290
to help me find you.

07:11.520 --> 07:13.080
Call everyone out here.

07:13.100 --> 07:13.930
Help me find someone.

07:13.930 --> 07:14.590
President.

07:14.930 --> 07:15.540
Come over.

07:16.230 --> 07:16.690
Quick.

07:17.420 --> 07:18.080
President.

07:19.400 --> 07:20.050
Found him.

07:21.200 --> 07:21.790
It's him.

07:22.000 --> 07:23.620
It's him. It definitely is him.

07:22.040 --> 07:22.540
[Missing Person]

07:23.540 --> 07:29.440
[Discussing the past
and lamenting the present]

07:24.180 --> 07:26.210
He was here
listening to stories during the day.

07:26.210 --> 07:28.010
When he heard us talk about
the temple of the underworld by the sea,

07:28.010 --> 07:29.410
he ran away immediately.

07:29.690 --> 07:30.400
Take a look.

07:30.750 --> 07:32.870
Do these characters on it

07:33.310 --> 07:35.480
spell out the word...

07:36.450 --> 07:36.920
Plan—

07:37.200 --> 07:38.250
a set of decisions.

07:38.250 --> 07:38.780
Plot—

07:38.800 --> 07:39.530
conspiracy.

07:39.659 --> 07:40.130
Fake—

07:40.130 --> 07:40.690
disguise.

07:40.690 --> 07:41.120
ASAP—

07:41.120 --> 07:42.250
as soon as possible.

07:52.430 --> 07:53.330
This is a plot.

07:54.220 --> 07:55.390
I have a plan.

07:56.860 --> 07:57.950
I need to fake something.

07:57.950 --> 07:58.950
Come save me ASAP.

08:00.250 --> 08:01.660
Isn't your friend dead?

08:01.660 --> 08:03.050
Why would he s-say "ASAP"?

08:03.050 --> 08:04.300
He faked his death.

08:04.780 --> 08:05.910
Faked his death?

08:06.600 --> 08:09.200
There should be a way
to save him on these bills.

08:09.330 --> 08:09.790
Then...

08:10.180 --> 08:11.100
That's a lot of bills—

08:11.100 --> 08:12.800
how do you know which bill it is?

08:12.800 --> 08:14.080
During our training,

08:14.390 --> 08:15.990
we also used money for codes.

08:16.480 --> 08:17.660
We'd look at the serial numbers

08:17.660 --> 08:19.070
and arrange the bills in order.

08:19.070 --> 08:20.090
I get it.

08:20.230 --> 08:22.460
I have this habit too when keeping books.

08:22.460 --> 08:25.120
I like to arrange bills
by their serial numbers.

08:25.190 --> 08:26.810
You're a natural-born spy.

08:33.760 --> 08:35.159
Danan Telegraph Office.

08:35.590 --> 08:36.929
So it's Haili Bank.

08:37.289 --> 08:37.960
Cracks.

08:38.970 --> 08:39.750
Eye.

08:40.820 --> 08:41.220
Wait.

08:41.220 --> 08:42.400
Haili Bank?

08:42.789 --> 08:44.670
Cracks, eyes—what do those mean?

08:44.860 --> 08:45.890
Haili Bank...

08:46.740 --> 08:47.290
The Southern Archives

08:47.290 --> 08:48.810
has an outer defense mechanism

08:48.810 --> 08:50.140
right below Haili Bank.

08:51.220 --> 08:52.550
The Southern Archives?

08:54.210 --> 08:56.300
God is indeed looking out for me.

08:57.120 --> 08:58.630
Thank you, Cousin.

09:00.550 --> 09:01.700
For everything I owe you,

09:01.700 --> 09:03.560
I'll pay you back in the next life.

09:08.190 --> 09:09.500
Haili Bank.

09:11.960 --> 09:13.650
Plague, wait for me!

09:34.370 --> 09:35.520
Mr. Warner.

09:37.770 --> 09:39.010
The 3 miles around the Dong Mansion

09:39.010 --> 09:41.460
have been completely cleared.

09:41.460 --> 09:44.260
And there's a whole army out there
surrounding it.

09:45.370 --> 09:47.520
We can't stay any longer
in this mess.

09:47.770 --> 09:49.410
Pick up the men, we have to leave.

09:49.410 --> 09:50.010
All right.

09:50.390 --> 09:51.530
Mr. Warner,

09:51.940 --> 09:54.220
our deal hasn't been finalized yet.

09:54.960 --> 09:56.060
You're leaving?

09:56.080 --> 09:58.530
Aren't you after the treasure on the map?

09:58.980 --> 09:59.740
Miss Dong,

09:59.770 --> 10:02.720
you should be very clear
about the situation outside.

10:02.720 --> 10:03.920
It's very dangerous.

10:04.080 --> 10:05.220
Those treasures

10:05.220 --> 10:06.530
are not worth dying

10:06.530 --> 10:07.920
in a foreign land.

10:08.410 --> 10:09.220
Miss Dong,

10:09.220 --> 10:11.100
your enemy will not stop

10:11.670 --> 10:13.510
until you are dead.

10:15.170 --> 10:17.200
If my musketeers withdraw now,

10:17.200 --> 10:18.790
maybe everyone

10:18.790 --> 10:19.990
will be slaughtered.

10:25.410 --> 10:25.980
Come in.

10:48.220 --> 10:49.010
Move it.

11:03.160 --> 11:05.460
And I'll show you real wealth.

11:17.880 --> 11:19.570
What's exactly below here?

11:20.460 --> 11:21.720
It's just

11:22.210 --> 11:23.930
a vault of the Dong family.

11:25.160 --> 11:27.030
I've changed my mind.

11:27.340 --> 11:28.810
We are going to protect Miss Dong.

11:28.810 --> 11:29.770
Miss Dong,

11:30.410 --> 11:31.860
you will keep your promise, right?

11:31.860 --> 11:32.580
Of course.

11:33.060 --> 11:35.800
They have a thousand times
more troops than we do.

11:36.140 --> 11:38.500
We go head-on, we dead.

11:38.600 --> 11:40.390
Since your boss agreed,

11:40.420 --> 11:42.140
it means he knows we will win.

11:42.170 --> 11:43.520
My friends, we will win!

11:43.540 --> 11:44.480
With our treasure,

11:44.480 --> 11:45.270
with our guns—

11:45.270 --> 11:46.070
huh!

11:46.660 --> 11:47.280
Come on!

12:01.970 --> 12:03.510
Prepare to attack.

12:03.540 --> 12:04.000
Yes!

13:00.300 --> 13:02.000
Who the hell is this Miss Dong?

13:02.030 --> 13:04.780
She even knows
how to deploy troops and fire.

13:06.290 --> 13:07.170
Those are some

13:07.170 --> 13:07.910
tricky shooting points

13:07.910 --> 13:08.510
she worked out.

13:08.510 --> 13:10.780
The hardest part is dealing
against the enemy.

13:10.780 --> 13:12.700
No, it's because of Maxim gun!

13:29.250 --> 13:31.710
I wonder where
the consulate people are now.

13:32.490 --> 13:33.850
Can they hold out?

13:43.970 --> 13:45.130
Ammunition loaded.

13:45.440 --> 13:46.000
Fire!

13:49.030 --> 13:50.000
Stand back!

13:55.510 --> 13:56.050
Fire!

14:01.090 --> 14:02.640
Stand back!

14:13.000 --> 14:14.300
Hurry up! Hurry up!

14:22.810 --> 14:25.460
[Haili Bank]

15:10.430 --> 15:10.890
Cousin.

15:10.910 --> 15:11.310
Why...

15:11.360 --> 15:12.860
Why are you here again?
Stop following me.

15:12.860 --> 15:13.260
You...

15:15.630 --> 15:16.200
If you dare call for help,

15:16.200 --> 15:17.660
I'll burn this place down.

15:17.700 --> 15:19.560
You know I'm capable of anything.

15:22.650 --> 15:24.310
Okay, I won't shout.

15:24.770 --> 15:25.460
But...

15:25.600 --> 15:26.820
You have to let me watch you.

15:26.820 --> 15:28.880
I'm going into the Archives with you.

16:06.540 --> 16:07.360
What are you doing?

16:07.360 --> 16:08.890
I should be asking you that.

16:09.360 --> 16:11.560
Mrs. Wesley, the manager of Haley Bank,

16:11.610 --> 16:13.070
is your great benefactor.

16:13.330 --> 16:14.730
If it wasn't for her help,

16:14.820 --> 16:17.100
you wouldn't have gotten
your friend's belongings.

16:17.100 --> 16:18.770
It's one thing not to repay her,

16:18.770 --> 16:19.790
but we shouldn't
bite the hand that feeds us

16:19.790 --> 16:21.050
and ruin her business.

16:27.010 --> 16:31.900
[Cracks] [Eyes]
[Chop (Cigarette brand)] [TB (Telegram)]

16:38.140 --> 16:38.980
I'm sorry.

16:43.350 --> 16:45.010
I sincerely apologize to you.

16:45.410 --> 16:46.470
I really shouldn't

16:47.480 --> 16:49.940
casually destroy
someone else's property.

16:52.790 --> 16:54.550
At least you have a conscience.

16:55.150 --> 16:56.270
You know me best.

16:59.340 --> 17:01.460
Trying to choke me unconscious
and ditch me again?

17:01.460 --> 17:02.300
No way.

17:02.550 --> 17:05.150
I've been practicing in secret
for a long time.

17:15.400 --> 17:18.730
Look closely for clues
about the cracks and the cigarettes.

18:27.490 --> 18:29.820
Don't... you have cigarettes right here?

18:30.420 --> 18:32.950
Could the cigarettes he mentioned

18:33.440 --> 18:35.700
mean something like a non-smoking area?

18:36.270 --> 18:37.330
I'm just guessing.

18:37.680 --> 18:40.340
Could the cigarettes
refer to the one in my hand?

19:40.670 --> 19:42.490
Looks like the vent is here.

19:51.770 --> 19:53.710
You knew I couldn't quit smoking.

19:54.900 --> 19:56.630
Here you are, still mocking me.

20:07.080 --> 20:07.520
No.

20:10.950 --> 20:11.390
Hey!

20:17.270 --> 20:18.200
There's a smell.

20:19.760 --> 20:20.560
What smell?

20:23.950 --> 20:24.760
Hard to say.

20:34.090 --> 20:37.090
[Double Cloud]

20:34.610 --> 20:36.030
Could this be the Southern Archives'

20:36.030 --> 20:37.690
defense mechanism entrance?

20:38.030 --> 20:40.360
Then what does the "eyes"
on the coin mean?

20:54.540 --> 20:57.270
There's indeed something wrong
with this crack.

21:04.710 --> 21:05.800
Be careful.

21:06.100 --> 21:07.290
Careful.

21:12.330 --> 21:13.390
What is this?

21:14.810 --> 21:15.540
Hard to tell.

21:16.400 --> 21:18.060
This belongs to Haili Bank.

21:18.090 --> 21:18.820
Give it to me.

21:19.700 --> 21:20.610
Give it.

21:21.070 --> 21:21.530
Hey!

21:23.940 --> 21:24.940
I'm warning you.

21:25.760 --> 21:27.130
When I go in later,

21:27.480 --> 21:28.540
stop following me.

21:28.730 --> 21:29.860
I can't protect you.

21:31.020 --> 21:31.650
I got it.

21:32.090 --> 21:33.150
You go first, or me?

21:33.190 --> 21:34.590
Forget it, I'll go first.

21:51.720 --> 21:52.870
Wait for me!

21:53.250 --> 21:55.200
Slow... Slow down!

21:55.960 --> 21:57.050
Wait for me!

21:59.250 --> 22:00.630
Slow down!

22:08.810 --> 22:10.280
You're really very lucky.

22:10.660 --> 22:11.530
There's a door here.

22:11.530 --> 22:12.350
It should be the exit.

22:12.350 --> 22:13.190
A door?

22:14.420 --> 22:15.140
We're finally here.

22:15.140 --> 22:15.600
Look.

22:16.330 --> 22:17.080
Right here.

22:17.430 --> 22:18.330
Let me see.

22:22.460 --> 22:23.460
Where is the door?

22:26.420 --> 22:27.160
Where?

22:27.510 --> 22:28.640
The door retreated.

22:29.590 --> 22:30.510
Retreated?

22:32.310 --> 22:33.840
What do you mean? I don't get it.

22:33.840 --> 22:34.790
When I was saw it,

22:34.790 --> 22:35.980
there was a door right here.

22:35.980 --> 22:36.680
But as soon as I turned my head,

22:36.680 --> 22:38.610
the door disappeared and ran away.

22:43.320 --> 22:45.380
You're terrible at lying now.

22:45.410 --> 22:46.330
I might not be smart,

22:46.330 --> 22:47.700
but I'm not stupid.

22:48.550 --> 22:49.550
Stop trying to fool me.

22:49.550 --> 22:50.550
I'm not leaving.

22:50.550 --> 22:51.660
I already told you.

22:52.370 --> 22:53.550
Wait for me.

22:56.460 --> 22:56.870
Look,

22:57.510 --> 22:59.040
there really is a door here.

22:59.620 --> 23:00.450
This is it.

23:00.920 --> 23:01.570
Door...

23:02.940 --> 23:03.810
my foot!

23:05.500 --> 23:06.720
Can you stop messing with me?

23:06.720 --> 23:07.940
There was definitely a door here just now.

23:07.940 --> 23:09.050
A white jade door,

23:09.050 --> 23:10.010
carved with patterns.

23:10.010 --> 23:11.780
But as soon as you came, it ran away.

23:11.780 --> 23:12.670
Alright.

23:17.550 --> 23:18.300
I got it.

23:19.520 --> 23:20.940
There's something wrong with your face.

23:20.940 --> 23:22.350
Every time I look back at your face

23:22.350 --> 23:24.210
and turn around, the door is gone.

23:24.340 --> 23:25.400
Or maybe this door

23:25.610 --> 23:27.410
needs to be watched all the time.

23:28.070 --> 23:29.360
Seriously?

23:29.380 --> 23:30.780
That's a personal attack.

23:30.780 --> 23:32.900
You're the one
with something wrong with your face.

23:32.900 --> 23:35.720
Plague, slow down! Wait for me!

23:37.600 --> 23:38.350
Go.

23:38.720 --> 23:39.310
Hurry up.

23:41.470 --> 23:42.470
I see the door.

23:43.990 --> 23:44.560
Quick.

23:45.150 --> 23:46.680
Hold the flashlight for me.

23:54.850 --> 23:56.110
There really is a door.

23:56.740 --> 23:57.740
What should we do?

23:57.930 --> 23:59.260
Is it because I blinked?

24:02.310 --> 24:02.830
Look.

24:05.920 --> 24:06.790
Wait, wait, wait.

24:06.790 --> 24:07.990
Let me think about it.

24:10.340 --> 24:11.990
[Eyes]

24:13.660 --> 24:15.790
I think I know the secret to this thing.

24:15.880 --> 24:16.780
It needs us

24:17.070 --> 24:18.500
to keep staring at it

24:18.530 --> 24:19.330
without blinking ever

24:19.330 --> 24:20.130
to capture it.

24:20.270 --> 24:20.850
Cousin.

24:21.170 --> 24:22.110
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

24:22.110 --> 24:22.910
I'll open the door.

24:22.910 --> 24:23.650
Wait.

24:25.550 --> 24:27.040
Let me try.

24:28.190 --> 24:28.930
Can you do it?

24:48.020 --> 24:48.860
Still there, still there, still there.

24:48.860 --> 24:50.260
You didn't blink, right?

24:50.340 --> 24:51.210
I didn't.

24:51.700 --> 24:52.310
I got it.

25:14.610 --> 25:16.780
There's a draft through the door.

25:38.290 --> 25:39.890
Plague, Plague, Plague.

25:41.460 --> 25:42.900
Come, come, come!

25:44.480 --> 25:45.440
I'm coming!

25:49.940 --> 25:52.010
You smashed my hand!

25:52.240 --> 25:52.680
I...

26:37.410 --> 26:39.210
Are you trying to kill yourself?

26:41.530 --> 26:42.360
Are you okay?

26:44.430 --> 26:45.410
I'm fine.

26:45.770 --> 26:47.630
Looks like we found the Archives.

26:48.650 --> 26:49.380
Get up.

26:52.130 --> 26:53.380
They're in the yard already.

26:53.380 --> 26:54.770
The machine guns in the secret passage

26:54.770 --> 26:56.060
have all been set up.

26:56.090 --> 26:57.960
Even if the consulate's reinforcements
don't arrive,

26:57.960 --> 26:59.150
as long as they enter the passage,

26:59.150 --> 27:00.110
within half an hour,

27:00.110 --> 27:01.740
I can kill them all.

27:02.250 --> 27:03.380
What's the situation out there?

27:03.380 --> 27:04.510
Three of our men died.

27:04.510 --> 27:06.420
Thirty-seven servants have been resettled.

27:06.420 --> 27:08.180
Two of them inhaled a poison gas,

27:08.180 --> 27:09.840
and they aren't looking good.

27:10.060 --> 27:11.180
Thirty-seven?

27:11.390 --> 27:14.050
Doesn't the Dong Mansion
only have 36 servants?

27:31.740 --> 27:34.360
Tell everyone
to enter that secret basement

27:34.500 --> 27:35.970
and stay on alert.

27:42.660 --> 27:43.510
Be careful!

28:33.220 --> 28:34.390
My daughter...

28:34.420 --> 28:35.350
Don't talk.

28:35.820 --> 28:38.620
I'll find someone
to stop your bleeding right now.

28:39.960 --> 28:42.150
You'll be on your own from now on.

28:44.010 --> 28:46.140
You must take good care of yourself.

28:47.140 --> 28:50.390
You have to live well.

29:26.740 --> 29:28.520
I have lived for way too long.

29:42.820 --> 29:43.750
Into the tunnel.

30:42.670 --> 30:43.950
Tear down

30:44.830 --> 30:46.580
this entire room.

30:48.130 --> 30:50.400
Don't leave a single piece
of the wall intact.

30:50.400 --> 30:51.060
-Yes!
-Yes!

30:55.680 --> 30:56.440
Plague!

30:57.270 --> 30:57.960
Wait for me!

30:58.570 --> 30:59.570
Hurry up, Cousin.

31:00.570 --> 31:01.770
Weren't you pretty strong just now?

31:01.770 --> 31:03.030
You even saved my life.

31:03.220 --> 31:04.020
Your reaction speed

31:04.020 --> 31:05.760
is much faster than before.

31:07.580 --> 31:09.360
I still have a conscience,

31:09.700 --> 31:10.660
unlike you

31:11.410 --> 31:12.540
who's so heartless.

31:13.560 --> 31:14.810
Let's take a break.

31:18.150 --> 31:19.750
Now I just need to follow these clues

31:19.750 --> 31:21.150
to find what I want.

31:21.440 --> 31:22.430
Sure, sure.

31:22.940 --> 31:25.440
Let's find it
and get out of here as soon as possible.

31:25.440 --> 31:25.970
Let's go.

31:58.280 --> 31:59.710
Is this the entrance?

32:14.930 --> 32:17.390
This is the only door
at the end of the tunnel.

32:24.420 --> 32:26.200
It's locked. We need a key.

32:26.390 --> 32:27.830
Let's not look for the key.

32:27.830 --> 32:29.890
Why don't we just force the door open?

32:32.150 --> 32:33.080
I smell sulfur.

32:33.950 --> 32:35.610
There are explosives inside.

32:36.900 --> 32:37.730
It's true.

32:38.350 --> 32:39.440
If someone tries to pry the door open

32:39.440 --> 32:40.560
or blow it up with explosives,

32:40.560 --> 32:42.220
they'd be blown to pieces too.

32:42.680 --> 32:44.280
We still need to find the key.

32:47.720 --> 32:49.010
Where do we find it?

32:56.270 --> 32:56.870
Anything?

32:59.270 --> 33:00.370
Inside here

33:01.070 --> 33:02.470
are fragments of the key.

33:08.620 --> 33:10.620
There are key fragments in here too.

33:10.830 --> 33:12.400
They look a lot like yours.

33:13.970 --> 33:15.570
Are they in every single one?

33:16.480 --> 33:17.280
My God.

33:17.760 --> 33:18.760
There are so many.

33:19.720 --> 33:21.190
You can't even tell the fragments apart.

33:21.190 --> 33:23.130
Isn't this to keep people out on purpose?

33:23.130 --> 33:25.070
This is the secret entrance
to the Archives.

33:25.070 --> 33:27.200
How could they let people in so easily?

33:27.380 --> 33:28.050
True.

33:29.530 --> 33:31.370
Look at the bills from your friend.

33:31.370 --> 33:33.400
There seem to be many symbol clues on it

33:33.400 --> 33:34.500
that we haven't used yet.

33:34.500 --> 33:35.260
No need.

33:35.280 --> 33:36.880
I've already figured it out.

33:42.950 --> 33:44.190
Are you sure?

33:44.470 --> 33:47.000
There are thousands of
possible arrangements for these fragments.

33:47.000 --> 33:48.970
How long will it take you to solve it?

33:48.970 --> 33:49.900
Clam down.

33:53.300 --> 33:54.990
What would Shrimpie do?

33:58.740 --> 34:00.070
This is a dead end.

34:00.070 --> 34:01.940
This is a scam.

34:02.700 --> 34:03.440
I doubt Southern Archives

34:03.440 --> 34:05.610
is here at all.

34:08.710 --> 34:09.400
I got it.

34:11.409 --> 34:12.210
It's the plot.

34:21.210 --> 34:22.420
How is it?

34:22.600 --> 34:23.929
Have you figured it out?

34:24.400 --> 34:27.000
Any of the keys can open both locks.

34:36.850 --> 34:38.650
Mentor, I think this test is a bit...

34:38.650 --> 34:39.610
not worth it.

34:39.610 --> 34:40.760
You only have two disciples.

34:40.760 --> 34:42.100
One of us will end up disabled.

34:42.100 --> 34:43.360
If we are disabled,

34:43.650 --> 34:44.440
you have no one left to torture.

34:44.440 --> 34:45.800
You two aren't that important.

34:45.800 --> 34:46.610
I don't care.

34:46.830 --> 34:47.310
I...

34:49.929 --> 34:51.659
Shrimpie is pretty important.

34:51.840 --> 34:52.960
I think this game

34:52.960 --> 34:54.420
isn't a test of skill at all.

34:54.420 --> 34:56.010
It's about who has a tougher life.

34:56.010 --> 34:57.650
There's no need to deceive our feelings.

34:57.650 --> 34:58.150
Right?

34:58.610 --> 34:59.920
Mentor, I got it.

35:00.210 --> 35:02.010
You just want us to make a choice.

35:02.170 --> 35:02.670
Right.

35:03.440 --> 35:04.230
But

35:07.460 --> 35:08.420
the time you have to choose is limited.

35:08.420 --> 35:08.940
Mentor!

35:11.440 --> 35:12.940
Is Mentor dating someone recently?

35:12.940 --> 35:15.470
Why is she getting
more and more mischievous?

35:19.810 --> 35:20.870
What are you doing?

35:21.050 --> 35:21.630
I'm fast.

35:21.630 --> 35:22.360
I can get the key.

35:22.360 --> 35:23.890
Your hand will be crippled!

35:26.140 --> 35:26.840
I get it.

35:28.270 --> 35:29.120
It's a plot.

35:38.440 --> 35:39.090
Run!

35:49.880 --> 35:51.610
When you face a dilemma in the future,

35:51.610 --> 35:53.100
step back and think about it first.

35:53.100 --> 35:53.840
See if you

35:53.840 --> 35:56.170
have already fallen into someone's plot.

35:58.000 --> 35:59.640
It's just a mind trap.

35:59.790 --> 36:01.950
There's an obvious man-made dilemma.

36:02.570 --> 36:04.410
Cousin, look at that door.

36:04.440 --> 36:06.290
It looks like a door on the surface,

36:06.290 --> 36:07.620
but it actually isn't.

36:07.690 --> 36:08.360
Or rather,

36:08.420 --> 36:10.280
it doesn't want to let you in at all.

36:10.280 --> 36:12.280
Normal people would stand in front
of the Bronze Ball Mechanism

36:12.280 --> 36:13.630
and think for weeks.

36:14.940 --> 36:15.940
But in actuality,

36:16.860 --> 36:18.400
it isn't an entrance at all.

36:19.400 --> 36:21.230
But these puzzles make people feel

36:21.230 --> 36:22.580
that if they think a little longer,

36:22.580 --> 36:24.240
they can find the real answer.

36:24.450 --> 36:25.800
So they get trapped here.

36:25.800 --> 36:27.280
When people think
in one place for too long,

36:27.280 --> 36:28.610
they easily sink into it

36:28.780 --> 36:29.870
and find it hard to change course.

36:29.870 --> 36:31.410
Only a very few geniuses

36:32.070 --> 36:33.270
can think in reverse.

36:33.920 --> 36:35.180
Like me, for instance.

36:35.630 --> 36:36.530
So?

36:37.510 --> 36:38.280
So, cousin,

36:39.830 --> 36:41.430
we should search in reverse.

36:42.290 --> 36:43.060
Reverse?

36:44.500 --> 36:45.780
We're going back?

36:45.800 --> 36:47.050
Are you crazy?

36:48.450 --> 36:49.300
Plague!

36:49.330 --> 36:51.440
I just got bandaged!

36:56.820 --> 36:57.830
Are you crazy?

36:58.420 --> 37:00.380
Searching in reverse
doesn't mean walking backward.

37:00.380 --> 37:00.940
Shush.

37:10.000 --> 37:12.730
If you're that good,
walk backward over this too.

37:14.650 --> 37:15.400
Seriously.

37:36.590 --> 37:37.760
You're stuck?

38:01.450 --> 38:03.180
The power of reverse thinking.

38:05.480 --> 38:07.030
Not bad at all.

38:28.000 --> 38:29.340
Is this what you called

38:29.750 --> 38:32.030
the Southern Archives?

38:32.480 --> 38:33.790
Finally found it.

38:45.110 --> 38:46.040
What's going on?

39:15.770 --> 39:16.400
Careful!

40:23.740 --> 40:24.840
So magnificent.
